{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1573125183,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MTkyMDA2OTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3859","origin":"github"},"title":"Dedicated DataLad \u003c--\u003e git-annex test suite","message":"DataLad is built on git-annex.It doesn't utilize all its features, but requires a substantial variety of them and a particular behavior. ATM we discover breakage of our (implicit) set of assumptions, when DataLad itself breaks due to behavior changes in git-annex.\n\nI believe it would be mutually beneficial to work towards formalizing what exactly DataLad expects from git-annex, and to test that without involving DataLad itself.\n\nI have no idea yet how to approach this best, but it would already move us forward to establish a spot for such tests, and add one whenever we observe this kind of breakage the traditional way.","files":null}]}